}}},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Reconcile whether the model's own bounded-COMMIT met=false (record_criterion_verdict at the third-evidence boundary, banking.py:544) is exhaustion vs. refutation, and state how the plan distinguishes it — either route that boundary through a marker-aware write too, or justify (positive rationale) why only the framework fallback_record path carries evidence_sufficient:false while the model-commit path legitimately banks a bare met=false.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.2,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["completion_banking.py:544 tool docstring: 'At that boundary, record `met=false` when evidence has not demonstrated MET' — a bounded-exhaustion outcome, not refutation","Plan: 'record_criterion_verdict's model-facing signature (:539) stays BOOL — the marker is policy-side only'","Problem statement targets 'budget ran out before sufficient evidence was found', which is exactly the model-commit-boundary case too, not only the fallback"],"finding":"The plan attaches the evidence_sufficient marker only to the framework fallback_record write path, but the model's own record_criterion_verdict tool ALSO banks met=false at the bounded-COMMIT boundary for 'evidence has not demonstrated MET' (banking.py:544) — which is itself absence-of-evidence, not refutation. Keeping that tool bool-only means model-committed-unmet entries bank a BARE met=false indistinguishable from genuine refutation, so the named problem (misattributing absence-of-evidence as evidence-of-absence) is only partly solved.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f76878418fd914214","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Proposed fix — completion_tool_policy.py fallback_record; completion_banking.py record_criterion_verdict (:539-544); AC 'A genuine positive refutation still banks met=false'","norm_id":"n17c5fa28eb5f0bb4","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Model reaches the third-evidence-call COMMIT boundary and records met=false without having refuted the criterion; this banks a bare met=false and yields an unmet-criterion FAIL — the same false-FAIL class the plan aims to eliminate."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify in the finalizer prompt (:23-28) the severity an insufficient-evidence (exhaustion) finding must carry, distinguishing it from the high-severity finding used for a genuine refutation.","cohort":["T8"],"criteria":["T8"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.398,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Prompt :26: 'Include one high-severity finding for every criterion with met: false.'","Plan: 'banked insufficient entries echo as met:false with insufficient findings text' — names the text but not the severity","Plan: 'stamp = enforcement, prompt = text alignment' — the stamp re-stamps the marker, not the finding severity the finalizer produces"],"finding":"The finalizer prompt update (completion_verifier_finalizer.md :23-28) does not specify the SEVERITY an insufficient-evidence finding should carry, leaving the tool-free finalizer's decision rule ambiguous. The current prompt mandates 'one high-severity finding for every criterion with met:false' (:26); the plan says insufficient entries echo 'with insufficient findings text' but never states whether those findings stay high-severity or take a distinct severity — the executor (the finalization LLM) has no rule to follow, and the deterministic re-stamp in merge_finalizer_with_bank only fixes the marker, not the finding text/severity the finalizer itself emits.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f7561be0164ae4e97","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Proposed fix — Finalizer prompt (completion_verifier_finalizer.md:23-28); prompt line :26","norm_id":"nf66a7540f4a042e2","priority":0.402,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A criterion whose evidence was not reached at exhaustion is echoed by the finalizer; the LLM cannot tell whether to emit high-severity or a lower/insufficient severity finding, so runs render inconsistent finding severities for the same insufficient class."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"In the finalizer prompt rule, split the finding directive: keep 'one high-severity finding' for genuinely refuted (met:false with contradictory evidence) criteria, and specify the severity/wording for insufficient (missing/truncated/unreached) evidence — or state that the finalizer emits the insufficient finding text and merge_finalizer_with_bank normalizes severity, whichever the design intends.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_ne